{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;message&quot;:{&quot;role&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:[{&quot;tool_use_id&quot;:&quot;toolu_01LQ9fDQVdFwD278NNE7CAqB&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;tool_result&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:&quot;AGENTS.md\nLICENSE\nREADME.md\nblockdoc\nblocks\ncatalog.xml\ndocs\nnode_modules\norg.blockml.bml.bom.Library.fat.bml\norg.blockml.bml.cli.Library.fat.bml\norg.blockml.bml.compiler.parser.Library.fat.bml\norg.blockml.bml.compiler.runtime.Library.fat.bml\norg.blockml.bml.compiler.serializer.Library.fat.bml\norg.blockml.bml.compiler.validator.Library.fat.bml\norg.blockml.bml.framework.Library.fat.bml\norg.blockml.bml.lsp.Library.fat.bml\norg.blockml.bml.target.blockdoc.Library.fat.bml\norg.blockml.bml.target.fatblock.Library.fat.bml\norg.blockml.bml.target.xsd.Library.fat.bml\norg.blockml.bml.workspace.Library.fat.bml\npackage-lock.json\npackage.json\npackages\nschemas\nscripts\ntests\ntsconfig.base.json\ntsconfig.json\nvitest.config.ts\n---\nUsage: blockml &lt;command> [options]\n       blockml --help\n\nblockml is the BlockML toolchain CLI.\n\nBML is the editable source of truth. Companions (TypeScript, HTML, XSD, …) are derived.\nChange BML first, then compile or edit companions to match. Do not invent model semantics.\n\nInvocation: npx blockml &lt;command>\nDo not install or upgrade @blockml/cli unless asked. If the CLI is missing, run npm ci.\nIf @blockml/cli is not a project dependency, report that and stop.\n\nDiscover the model with the CLI, not grep:\n  search    where something is (find FQNs)\n  inspect   give me this Block already resolved (effective members)\n  graph     how it connects (inheritance, uses, used-by)\nGeneric grep, find, and file reads remain allowed. They are not the first way into the model.\n\nWorkflow:\n  task → search → FQNs → inspect (graph if structure) → targeted BML read → smallest BML edit → validate\n       → update companions to match (compile and/or edit)\n\nCommands:\n  search      Find FQNs. Corpus is validate --all.\n              blockml search &lt;query> [--json] [--limit n]\n              blockml search index [--force]\n  inspect     Resolved Block JSON (effective members).\n              blockml inspect &lt;fqn> [--depth n]\n  graph       Inheritance, uses / used-by, members, paths.\n              blockml graph uses|used-by|neighbors|ancestors|descendants|members &lt;fqn>\n              blockml graph path &lt;from> &lt;to>\n              blockml graph query &lt;cypher> | schema | index\n  new         Create a Block .bml and export it from the owning Library.\n              blockml new &lt;fqn> [--baseType FQN] [--is text]\n  validate    Parser + semantic check. Default: project sources, not npm.\n              blockml validate [--all] [&lt;file>]\n  compile     Render derived output for a registered target.\n              blockml compile blockdoc|xsd|fatblock\n  transform   Run a pending ModelTransformation.\n              blockml transform apply &lt;execution-fqn>\n\nShared flags: --src dir, --libraries a,b, --json, --help / -h\nCorpus for search, inspect, and graph is the same as validate --all.\nExit codes: 0 success, 1 diagnostic errors, 2 usage or configuration error.\n\nRun `blockml &lt;command> --help` for flags, defaults, output, and constraints.&quot;,&quot;is_error&quot;:false}]},&quot;parent_tool_use_id&quot;:null,&quot;session_id&quot;:&quot;6d7ee702-e917-4dda-9026-4533011ce3b2&quot;,&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;73e29761-2154-4b89-8d35-c6777282c7c7&quot;,&quot;timestamp&quot;:&quot;2026-09-03T20:36:35.007Z&quot;,&quot;tool_use_result&quot;:{&quot;stdout&quot;:&quot;AGENTS.md\nLICENSE\nREADME.md\nblockdoc\nblocks\ncatalog.xml\ndocs\nnode_modules\norg.blockml.bml.bom.Library.fat.bml\norg.blockml.bml.cli.Library.fat.bml\norg.blockml.bml.compiler.parser.Library.fat.bml\norg.blockml.bml.compiler.runtime.Library.fat.bml\norg.blockml.bml.compiler.serializer.Library.fat.bml\norg.blockml.bml.compiler.validator.Library.fat.bml\norg.blockml.bml.framework.Library.fat.bml\norg.blockml.bml.lsp.Library.fat.bml\norg.blockml.bml.target.blockdoc.Library.fat.bml\norg.blockml.bml.target.fatblock.Library.fat.bml\norg.blockml.bml.target.xsd.Library.fat.bml\norg.blockml.bml.workspace.Library.fat.bml\npackage-lock.json\npackage.json\npackages\nschemas\nscripts\ntests\ntsconfig.base.json\ntsconfig.json\nvitest.config.ts\n---\nUsage: blockml &lt;command> [options]\n       blockml --help\n\nblockml is the BlockML toolchain CLI.\n\nBML is the editable source of truth. Companions (TypeScript, HTML, XSD, …) are derived.\nChange BML first, then compile or edit companions to match. Do not invent model semantics.\n\nInvocation: npx blockml &lt;command>\nDo not install or upgrade @blockml/cli unless asked. If the CLI is missing, run npm ci.\nIf @blockml/cli is not a project dependency, report that and stop.\n\nDiscover the model with the CLI, not grep:\n  search    where something is (find FQNs)\n  inspect   give me this Block already resolved (effective members)\n  graph     how it connects (inheritance, uses, used-by)\nGeneric grep, find, and file reads remain allowed. They are not the first way into the model.\n\nWorkflow:\n  task → search → FQNs → inspect (graph if structure) → targeted BML read → smallest BML edit → validate\n       → update companions to match (compile and/or edit)\n\nCommands:\n  search      Find FQNs. Corpus is validate --all.\n              blockml search &lt;query> [--json] [--limit n]\n              blockml search index [--force]\n  inspect     Resolved Block JSON (effective members).\n              blockml inspect &lt;fqn> [--depth n]\n  graph       Inheritance, uses / used-by, members, paths.\n              blockml graph uses|used-by|neighbors|ancestors|descendants|members &lt;fqn>\n              blockml graph path &lt;from> &lt;to>\n              blockml graph query &lt;cypher> | schema | index\n  new         Create a Block .bml and export it from the owning Library.\n              blockml new &lt;fqn> [--baseType FQN] [--is text]\n  validate    Parser + semantic check. Default: project sources, not npm.\n              blockml validate [--all] [&lt;file>]\n  compile     Render derived output for a registered target.\n              blockml compile blockdoc|xsd|fatblock\n  transform   Run a pending ModelTransformation.\n              blockml transform apply &lt;execution-fqn>\n\nShared flags: --src dir, --libraries a,b, --json, --help / -h\nCorpus for search, inspect, and graph is the same as validate --all.\nExit codes: 0 success, 1 diagnostic errors, 2 usage or configuration error.\n\nRun `blockml &lt;command> --help` for flags, defaults, output, and constraints.&quot;,&quot;stderr&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;interrupted&quot;:false,&quot;isImage&quot;:false,&quot;noOutputExpected&quot;:false}}
